WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.918
Deterministic Simulation

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.743
Testing is for

00:00:02.661 --> 00:00:03.333
everyone

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.760
not just distributed

00:00:04.572 --> 00:00:05.361
systems

00:00:05.886 --> 00:00:07.112
An essay arguing

00:00:06.924 --> 00:00:07.949
that deterministic

00:00:07.761 --> 00:00:08.963
simulation testing

00:00:09.164 --> 00:00:10.367
usually associated

00:00:10.178 --> 00:00:11.805
with distributed databases

00:00:11.983 --> 00:00:12.902
is a practical

00:00:12.714 --> 00:00:13.952
testing technique for

00:00:13.905 --> 00:00:15.013
any application

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:16.316
If the bug

00:00:16.128 --> 00:00:16.965
can no longer

00:00:16.776 --> 00:00:17.766
be reproduced

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.698
we have proven

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:19.559
to ourselves that

00:00:19.371 --> 00:00:20.597
the test corresponds

00:00:20.409 --> 00:00:21.127
to the bug

00:00:21.316 --> 00:00:22.094
and we keep

00:00:21.906 --> 00:00:22.625
the test to

00:00:22.437 --> 00:00:23.639
guard against further

00:00:23.451 --> 00:00:24.335
regressions

00:00:24.854 --> 00:00:26.339
Doubting every development

00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:27.177
decision we make

00:00:26.988 --> 00:00:27.990
is exhausting

00:00:28.129 --> 00:00:29.061
I argue that

00:00:28.872 --> 00:00:29.615
it's a testing

00:00:29.427 --> 00:00:30.782
technique for everyone

00:00:30.606 --> 00:00:32.103
and all applications

00:00:32.646 --> 00:00:33.660
Full story on

00:00:33.471 --> 00:00:34.367
the dashboard
